Package: cIPMA
Type: Package
Title: Combined Importance-Performance Map Analysis
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person("Marek", "Deja", email = "marek.deja@uj.edu.pl",
    role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-0015-2322"))
Description: Combines the importance-performance map analysis (IPMA) of
    partial least squares structural equation modelling (PLS-SEM), estimated
    with 'seminr', with Quantile Necessary Condition Analysis (QNCA) of each
    predictor, following the combined importance-performance map analysis
    (cIPMA) of Hauff et al. (2024) <doi:10.1016/j.jretconser.2024.103723>.
    Necessity is decided at the strict limit, where the QNCA frontier equals
    the ceiling envelopment-free disposal hull (CE-FDH) ceiling of Necessary
    Condition Analysis (NCA) of Dul (2016) <doi:10.1177/1094428115584005>, and
    a tolerance sets the share of successful cases allowed below each
    bottleneck. The package reports the combined map, the bottleneck at a
    target level, the path of effect sizes and bottlenecks across tolerances,
    the QNCA diagnostics, assumption checks (reliability,
    heterotrait-monotrait ratio, variance inflation factor) and plots on a
    zoomed or a full scale. Exploratory structure learning with 'bnlearn' is
    available as an experimental option.
